{#
sharing/booking_page.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
A published booking page: what the appointment is, when it is free, and the
form that takes one.

**What is on screen is what is free right now.** `week` was built from slots
BookingAvailabilityReader produced against the owner's real diary at the instant
this request arrived — an event they created a minute ago has already removed
its slot, and one they cancelled has already brought it back. Nothing is cached
and nothing is client-side, because a stale slot list is a page that offers
appointments it cannot honour.

**Nothing here says why a slot is missing.** The page renders BookableSlot,
which carries an instant and a length and nothing else, so a gap in the morning
is indistinguishable from an hour outside the working day, and an empty column
is indistinguishable from a day off. That is the same rule the shared calendar
keeps, for the same reason: whoever holds this URL is not entitled to read the
owner's diary out of the shape of the holes in it.

**Three display parameters, and none of them is real.** The `tz` in the URL and
the hidden `timeZone` field change how the hours are PRINTED; `w` changes which
week is on screen; the owner's theme changes the colours. Which slots exist is
decided in the owner's zone, server-side, and no query parameter can move one —
see BookingController::displayZone() and BookingWeekBuilder, and see
BookingAvailabilityReader::findFreeSlot(), which re-derives the posted slot and
is the thing actually standing between this page and "book any hour you like".

No CSRF token, deliberately: this page starts no session, and rendering one
would. BookingController's docblock has the argument in full.

── A week, not a scroll ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Every free day between now and the horizon used to be rendered at once, which is
thirty headings on a default page and reads as a list of times rather than as a
calendar. A week is the unit people decide in, it fits seven columns on a laptop
and seven rows on a phone, and it gives the page the control it was missing:
somewhere to go when this week does not suit. Every day of the chosen week is
drawn, including the ones with nothing on them, because "no times on Wednesday"
has to be something the page says.

Variables:
  page        BookingPage                     the appointment being offered
  token       string                          this page's own URL segment
  days        array<string, BookableSlot[]>   every free slot, keyed Y-m-d in `zone`
  week        BookingWeek                     the seven days on screen, and the steps
  weekParam   string                          the query/form key naming a week
  zone        string                          the IANA zone the hours are printed in
  appearance  PublicAppearance                the owner's theme
  timeFormat  string                          a PHP date() format, from the install's clock
  errorKey    string|null                     a translation key for a refusal
  error       string|null                     a refusal already written for a person
  wasTaken    bool                            the last attempt lost the race
  name        string                          echoed back after a refusal
  email       string                          echoed back after a refusal
  note        string                          echoed back after a refusal
#}
{% extends 'sharing/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ page.name }}{% endblock %}

{% block container_class %}max-w-3xl{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    {# The browser's own zone, put in the URL once so the server can print the
       hours on the reader's clock. A reload rather than client-side rewriting:
       the slot instants are the server's, and re-rendering them in JavaScript
       is a second implementation of the same formatting to disagree with. The
       guard is what stops it looping — with `tz` already set, this does
       nothing. #}
    <script>
        (function () {
            const url = new URL(window.location.href);

            if (url.searchParams.has("tz")) {
                return;
            }

            const zone = Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone;

            if (zone) {
                url.searchParams.set("tz", zone);
                window.location.replace(url.toString());
            }
        })();
    </script>

    <header class="rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-4 sm:px-5 sm:py-5">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent/10 text-accent"
                  aria-hidden="true">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar-check"></i>
            </span>

            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <h1 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{{ page.name }}</h1>

                <div class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-sunken px-2.5 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                        <i class="fa-regular fa-hourglass-half text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.duration'|trans({ '%count%': page.slotMinutes }) }}
                    </span>

                    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-sunken px-2.5 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                        <i class="fa-regular fa-clock text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.zone'|trans({ '%zone%': zone }) }}
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        {% if page.description is not empty %}
            <p class="mt-3 whitespace-pre-line text-sm text-ink-muted">{{ page.description }}</p>
        {% endif %}
    </header>

    {% if wasTaken %}
        <div role="alert" class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-2.5 rounded-lg alert-danger px-3.5 py-3 text-sm text-danger">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p class="leading-snug">{{ 'calendar.booking.error.taken'|trans }}</p>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if errorKey is not null or error is not null %}
        <div role="alert" class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-2.5 rounded-lg alert-danger px-3.5 py-3 text-sm text-danger">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p class="leading-snug">{{ errorKey is not null ? errorKey|trans : error }}</p>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if days is empty %}
        <p class="mt-6 rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-10 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
            {{ 'calendar.booking.no_slots'|trans }}
        </p>
    {% else %}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_booking_book', { token: token }) }}" class="mt-6 space-y-5">
            <input type="hidden" name="timeZone" value="{{ zone }}">
            {# The week travels with the post so a refusal comes back on the week
               the reader was looking at rather than on the first one offered. #}
            <input type="hidden" name="{{ weekParam }}" value="{{ week.startsOn|date('Y-m-d') }}">

            <fieldset class="rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface overflow-hidden">
                <legend class="sr-only">{{ 'calendar.booking.pick_a_time'|trans }}</legend>

                {# The same row the calendar's own toolbar is: where you are, and
                   the two ways out of it. A step past the notice period at one
                   end or the horizon at the other is drawn disabled rather than
                   removed, so the row does not change shape as you page — and so
                   the reader can see there is no more rather than wondering. #}
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border-b border-line min-h-[var(--pane-header-h)]">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0">
                        {% if week.previous is not null %}
                            <a href="{{ path('app_booking_show', { token: token, (weekParam): week.previous, tz: zone }) }}"
                               class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
                               aria-label="{{ 'calendar.nav.previous'|trans }}"
                            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-faint opacity-40"
                                  aria-hidden="true"
                            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left text-xs"></i></span>
                        {% endif %}

                        {% if week.next is not null %}
                            <a href="{{ path('app_booking_show', { token: token, (weekParam): week.next, tz: zone }) }}"
                               class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
                               aria-label="{{ 'calendar.nav.next'|trans }}"
                            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-faint opacity-40"
                                  aria-hidden="true"
                            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-xs"></i></span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>

                    {# The year is dropped from the near end when both ends share
                       it, and the month too when the week does not cross one —
                       the same rule calendar/_toolbar.html.twig applies to its
                       own week heading, so the two read alike. #}
                    {% set weekEnd = week.startsOn|date_modify('+6 days') %}
                    <h2 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink truncate min-w-0">
                        {{ week.startsOn|date(week.startsOn|date('Y') == weekEnd|date('Y')
                            ? (week.startsOn|date('n') == weekEnd|date('n') ? 'j' : 'j M')
                            : 'j M Y') }}
                        – {{ weekEnd|date('j M Y') }}
                    </h2>
                </div>

                {% if week.isEmpty %}
                    <p class="px-4 py-10 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.no_slots_this_week'|trans }}
                    </p>
                {% else %}
                    {# One column per day above `sm`, one block per day below it.
                       Seven columns of pills on a phone is four characters wide;
                       seven blocks is a scroll somebody can actually tap. #}
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-7 gap-px bg-line" data-booking-week>
                        {% for day in week.days %}
                            {# One background or the other, never both in the same
                               attribute: two `bg-*` utilities are resolved by
                               their order in the compiled stylesheet rather than
                               in the class list, so "today plus surface" is a
                               coin toss that changes when Tailwind is rebuilt. #}
                            {# A day that has already happened is dimmed, and that
                               is the only thing on this page that says why a
                               column is empty — because it is a fact about the
                               clock rather than about the owner's diary. Without
                               it, a page opened on a Friday begins with four
                               columns reading "nothing free", which looks like
                               somebody who blocked out their whole week. #}
                            <div data-booking-day="{{ day.date }}"
                                 {% if day.isPast %}data-booking-day-past{% endif %}
                                 class="px-3 py-2 sm:px-1.5 sm:py-2 {{ day.isToday ? 'bg-accent/5' : 'bg-surface' }}
                                        {{ day.isPast ? 'opacity-50' : '' }}">
                                <p class="mb-1.5 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide
                                          {{ day.isToday ? 'text-accent font-semibold' : 'text-ink-faint' }}">
                                    {{ day.date|date('D') }}
                                    <span class="tabular-nums">{{ day.date|date('j') }}</span>
                                </p>

                                {% if day.slots is empty %}
                                    <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint italic">
                                        {{ 'calendar.booking.day_none'|trans }}
                                    </p>
                                {% else %}
                                    <div class="flex flex-wrap sm:flex-col gap-1">
                                        {% for slot in day.slots %}
                                            {# A radio rather than a button per slot: the whole page is one
                                               form, so choosing a time and filling the fields below is one
                                               submit. A button per slot would post before the name and
                                               address existed, which is how a two-step booking flow with a
                                               second page to lose people on gets invented. #}
                                            {% set slotId = 'slot-' ~ loop.parent.loop.index ~ '-' ~ loop.index %}

                                            <label for="{{ slotId }}"
                                                   class="cursor-pointer text-center rounded-lg border border-field bg-field
                                                          px-2.5 py-1 text-xs tabular-nums text-ink-soft
                                                          transition-colors hover:bg-hover
                                                          has-[:checked]:border-accent has-[:checked]:bg-accent has-[:checked]:text-accent-ink">
                                                <input type="radio"
                                                       id="{{ slotId }}"
                                                       name="slot"
                                                       value="{{ slot.key }}"
                                                       required
                                                       class="sr-only">
                                                {{ slot.startsAt|date(timeFormat, zone) }}
                                            </label>
                                        {% endfor %}
                                    </div>
                                {% endif %}
                            </div>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </fieldset>

            <div class="rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-4 space-y-4">
                <div class="space-y-1.5">
                    <label for="booking-name" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.your_name'|trans }}
                    </label>
                    <input type="text"
                           id="booking-name"
                           name="name"
                           value="{{ name }}"
                           required
                           maxlength="120"
                           autocomplete="name"
                           class="w-full h-9 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                                  focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-1.5">
                    <label for="booking-email" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.your_email'|trans }}
                    </label>
                    <input type="email"
                           id="booking-email"
                           name="email"
                           value="{{ email }}"
                           required
                           maxlength="255"
                           autocomplete="email"
                           class="w-full h-9 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                                  focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">
                    <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.your_email_help'|trans }}
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-1.5">
                    <label for="booking-note" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
                        {{ 'calendar.booking.note'|trans }}
                    </label>
                    <textarea id="booking-note"
                              name="note"
                              rows="3"
                              maxlength="2000"
                              class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                                     focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">{{ note }}</textarea>
                </div>

                <button type="submit"
                        class="w-full sm:w-auto inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 h-10 px-5 rounded-lg
                               text-sm font-medium text-accent-ink bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong transition-colors">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-check text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'calendar.booking.confirm'|trans }}
                </button>
            </div>
        </form>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
